I prefer to have my magicbane enchanted higher (to +7 if i can, +6
otherwise). You can see jove's reasoning for enchanging magicbane
higher here:

http://www.mindspring.com/~jove/Spoilers/Magicbane.txt

and discussion here

http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/tree/browse_frm/thread/9bcd4fb9260c02ef/

So i think you're fine with +4 and i'd even try to go a little higher.

> 2. Soon after I found that problem, I got a Frost Brand from
> sacrificing.  Should I switch to Frost Brand, or should I stay with my
> +4 Magicbane?  I found there are a lot of debates over best Wizard
> weapon here.

I don't usually like to use frost brand because it destroys potions
when you hit an enemy (it freezes them). And i usually need potions. As
a wizard, if a monster is too tough to melee then i'll just throw
daggers or use magic missile which are my most potent attacks anyways.
I only use melee attack when i'm conserving mana and/or too lazy to
pick up daggers and when i know that it's safe to use melee.

> 3. I do not find a lot scroll of enchant armor along the way, so my AC
> is still -1.  While that seems enough for me now, I am afraid I can be
> easily taken out with one or two strikes by stronger monsters.  Should
> I keep venturing down the dungeon or should I stay where I am until I
> advanced to Exp14-15?

yes. -1 AC is very high. I'd drop all armor you find / have left around
on an altar to determine if it's blessed/uncursed/cursed and try every
uncursed/blessed piece on. You'll be suprised how often you find a +2
or +3 piece of armor, and even a +4 or +5. But -1 AC at this point is
very risky. Try to get it close to -15/-20 before you venture further.
Being at DL20 you will have plenty, plenty of armor to choose from and
i'd be suprised if you didn't find at least 1 +4 piece of armor.

